// rule B origin-keying regression — local Foo and package Foo both declare X with OPPOSITE value
// types. include "Foo" resolves qualified refs package-FIRST, so "Foo"."X" is the PACKAGE X
// (Quantity) — a valid value-comparison operand, so NO error. A name-keyed (origin-blind) type
// index would collide the two Foo libraries and could read the LOCAL X (boolean) -> a FALSE error.
library "Root".
include "Foo".

concept "Check":
- value type is boolean.
- definition is "Foo"."X" at least 30 'kg/m2'.
